## Result up front

The bounded append/history bridge is positive.

A complete current Record carries both a front `f` and its last outcome `b`.
When the one 32-site block immediately ahead is the exact radial Blank, that
Record selects a physical append instrument which

1. leaves the old Record unchanged;
2. prepares the forward live state from `b`;
3. writes one new permanent Record with outcome `c`;
4. disables the old location because its forward block is no longer Blank; and
5. returns the new location in the same input type, ready to accept the next
   supplied Blank.

The exact branch effect is

\[
 L^{x\dagger}_{fbc}L^x_{fbc}
 =T(c\mid b)\,C^x_{fb}\otimes B^{x+9f},                \tag{1}
\]

where `C^x_fb` is the complete current classical-Record control (with identity
on its six old live qubits), `B` is the exact complete Blank-block projector,
and `T(c|b)` is contracted from the physical preparation and positive root.
The runner does not assign a target transition table to (1).

For every fixed finite `n>=1`, fixed front, and outcome tuple, sequential
composition gives the cylinder effect

\[
 F^{(n)}_{b_1\ldots b_n}
 =E_{b_1}\prod_{j=1}^{n-1}T(b_{j+1}\mid b_j).          \tag{2}
\]

It is projectively consistent:

\[
 \sum_{b_n}F^{(n)}_{b_1\ldots b_n}
 =F^{(n-1)}_{b_1\ldots b_{n-1}},\qquad
 \sum_{b_1,\ldots,b_n}F^{(n)}_{b_1\ldots b_n}=I.       \tag{3}
\]

Equations (1)--(3) also hold after tensoring with an arbitrary external
reference identity. This is a genuine reusable local history mechanism on its
stated boundary, not merely a three-event lookup table.

