All site sequences are bound exactly. A hostile mutation which moves one
writer factor to the fake site `(99,99,99)` is rejected before it can inherit a
physical scalar or carrier certificate.

Summing the fourteen next-outcome Grams at one current control gives

\[
 \sum_c L^{x\dagger}_{fbc}L^x_{fbc}
 =C^x_{fb}\otimes B^{x+9f}.                             \tag{4}
\]

The 84 current controls are mutually orthogonal, so

\[
 P_x=\sum_{f,b}C^x_{fb}\otimes B^{x+9f},\qquad
 K_{\rm STOP}=I-P_x                                    \tag{5}
\]

satisfy `P_x^2=P_x` and

\[
 \sum_{f,b,c}L^{x\dagger}_{fbc}L^x_{fbc}
 +K_{\rm STOP}^{\dagger}K_{\rm STOP}=I.                \tag{6}
\]

Thus the instrument is CPTP on the complete fixed-anchor carrier, including
the STOP complement and `I_outside`. “Global” in the executed check means
complete on this anchored input Hilbert space; it does not mean a simultaneous
update on the whole lattice.

