## Self-delimiting returned tip

Before an append, the current Record at `x` and exact Blank at `x+9f` lie in
the valid sector of (5). After a success, the forward pointer is
`Locked_(f,c)`, orthogonal to the Blank pointer. Reapplying the old anchored
instrument therefore reaches STOP. The new Record at `x+9f`, however, has the
same complete type and selects `x+18f`; if that block is supplied Blank, the
translated instrument accepts it.

On an isolated straight chain, all earlier Record blocks have Locked forward
neighbors, while only the newest Record has the one supplied forward Blank.
The eligible set is therefore the unique tip. Every append acts as identity on
the current live qubits, all backward and lateral spectator sites, and all
older sites through `I_outside`.

The support span along the selected axis is eight while successive centers
are separated by nine. Hence every distinct block on the straight ray is
disjoint for arbitrary finite depth; this is an analytic support statement,
not an inference from a finite scan.

